-- Prove2me | Definitions.Def_BunkbedTransferClasses
-- name    : BunkbedTransferClasses
-- status  : Definition
-- author  : @burkh4rt
-- created : 2026-09-12T15:44:44.727814+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/44fe7226-6136-4fd3-b350-eb6d925a6567
-- title:
--   The fifteen level-1 classes of Hollom's hypergraph
-- statement:
--   The difference between the cross-level and the same-level connection probability on Hollom's hypergraph is the double sum $\sum_{\pi_0, \pi_1} \delta(\pi_0, \pi_1) W(\pi_0) W(\pi_1)$ over the $47 \times 47$ pairs of level profiles, where $\delta = [0@0 \leftrightarrow 9@1] - [0@0 \leftrightarrow 9@0]$.
--
--   Because the two levels interact only through the posts over $T = \{1, 6, 8\}$, the quantity $\delta(\pi_0, \pi_1)$ depends on $\pi_1$ only through its restriction to $\{1, 6, 8, 9\}$. That restriction takes **15** values, so the 47 level-$1$ profiles fall into 15 classes. Here `wk k` is the total weight of class $k$, and `ck k` is the level-$0$ contraction $\sum_j \delta(\pi_j, \text{class } k) \, W(\pi_j)$; both are homogeneous of degree $6$ in the Wierman--Ziff state probabilities $x = P_{abc}$, $y = P_{a|b|c}$, $z = P_{a|bc}$, $u = P_{ab|c} = P_{ac|b}$.
--
--   The difference polynomial is then simply $\sum_{k < 15} (\mathtt{ck}\,k)(\mathtt{wk}\,k)$ — fifteen products of degree-$6$ polynomials rather than the $695$ pairs on which $\delta$ is nonzero. Fifteen is not an accident: it is exactly the rank of the $47 \times 47$ integer matrix $\delta$.
--
--   Each polynomial is written as a sum of short pieces `_p0, _p1, ...`; this is purely an elaboration-cost measure, since a single long chain of monomial summands costs superlinearly to elaborate.
-- source:
--   Gladkov, Pak, Zimin, *The bunkbed conjecture is false*, PNAS 122 (2025) no. 24, e2420725122; Section 3, Hollom's 3-uniform hypergraph (Fig. 1) and the path $\rho$ of Eq. [5].

import Definitions.Def_BunkbedTransferTables

/-!
# The fifteen level-1 classes

The two levels of the bunkbed interact only through the posts over `T = {1,6,8}`, so whether
`0` on level 0 reaches `9` on either level depends on the level-1 profile only through its
restriction to `{1,6,8,9}`. That restriction takes **15** values, so the 47 level-1 profiles
fall into 15 classes. `wk k` is the total weight of class `k`, and `ck k` is the level-0
contraction `Σ_j δ(π_j, class k) W(π_j)`. The difference polynomial is then just
`Σ_{k<15} ck k * wk k` — fifteen products rather than the 695 nonzero pairs, 15 being
exactly the rank of the 47 × 47 matrix `δ`.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false

